    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Next step carries chunking of the loaded data.\n",
        "\n",
        "use splitline() to split text in to the list of individual lines splitted based on whitespaces(\\n). This also cleans up the extra spaces in the end of the lines so its better than text.split(\"\\n\")\n",
        "\n",
        "Once the text is converted to line. use strip method to remove whitespaces from front and back. also remove \"#\" character from the beginning to make the text cleaner for each line.\n",
        "\n",
        "splitted data is then iterated through to create a list of all the valid lines.\n",
        "\n",
        "Once the list is ready , its then combined ina single word with \"separator\".join method. here separateor is \" \". this is further converted to a list of all the words with .split().\n",
        "\n",
        "the function create_chunks takes the string with all the words (created and formatted after retreiving text from URL). It then creates a chunk which has a index and content. it eventually creates the list of chunks(dictionary) and returns."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "TiisUWzuQMVg"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "def create_chunks(test_data: str, chunk_size: int) -> list[dict]:\n",
        "  splitted_data = test_data.splitlines()\n",
        "  clean_data = []\n",
        "  for line in splitted_data:\n",
        "    if line:\n",
        "      clean_data.append(line.strip().lstrip(\"#\").strip())\n",
        "  words = \" \".join(clean_data).split()\n",
        "\n",
        "  chunks = []\n",
        "  for i in range(0, len(words), chunk_size):\n",
        "    content = \" \".join(words[i:i+chunk_size])\n",
        "    chunks.append({\n",
        "        \"chunk_index\": len(chunks),\n",
        "        \"content\" : content\n",
        "                   })\n",
        "  return(chunks)\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "-CKWMnCaQVPB"
      },
      "execution_count": 51,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "create chunk function execution"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "AUVZcD5_jU-9"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "created_chunks = create_chunks(raw_text, 50)\n",
        "print(created_chunks[32])\n",
        "print(len(created_chunks))"
      ],
